'''''Rosa mandonii''''' is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Rosaceae]], native to [[Madeira]].<ref name="POWO_733228-1" >{{cite POWO |id=733228-1 |title=''Rosa mandonii'' Déségl. |access-date=22 July 2023 }}</ref> Some authorities consider it to be indistinguishable from ''[[Rosa canina]]'', the dog rose.<ref name="ROSMW" >{{cite web |url=https://gd.eppo.int/taxon/ROSMW |title=''Rosa mandonii'' (ROSMW) |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2023 |website=EPPO Global Database |publisher=European and Mediterranean Plant Protection Organization |access-date=22 July 2023 }}</ref> It is most often found in the [[laurisilva]], but can also occur in other types of woodland and in thickets.<ref>{{cite book |title=Endemism in Vascular Plants |series=Plant and Vegetation |year=2014 |volume=9 |doi=10.1007/978-94-007-6913-7 |isbn=978-94-007-6912-0 |s2cid=38585096 }}</ref> 

